author: pi-agent
comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-29T04:45:17.227Z",pi-agent,"Confirmed all three findings. The assignment regex accepts adjacent hash prefixes, and textual scalar expansion can reinterpret operators and backslashes as scanner syntax."
  "2026-08-29T04:46:18.037Z",pi-agent,"Required whitespace before trailing # comments, rejected expansion values containing shell operators, decoded double-quoted escapes correctly, and protected expansion-produced backslashes. npm test passes (300 tests)."
  "2026-08-29T04:53:33.720Z",pi-agent,Follow-up review found multiline subshell scope leakage. shellScalars now tracks quote-aware parenthesis depth across lines and indexes assignments only at file scope; targeted regression passes.
  "2026-08-29T04:59:44.743Z",pi-agent,"Second follow-up: scope tracking now stops at an unquoted shell comment boundary, so comment prose cannot leak quote or parenthesis state. Audit-level regression passes."
  "2026-08-29T05:06:30.281Z",pi-agent,"Third follow-up: scalar-expanded attestation flags are now conservatively neutralized because static scope tracking cannot prove conditional/function execution; scalar-held commands remain expanded and audited. Full attestation verifier file passes (64 tests)."
  "2026-08-29T05:14:25.142Z",pi-agent,"Final scope model tracks functions, conditional bodies, subshells, comments, and quoted/unquoted heredoc bodies. Restored unconditional scalar attestation and prevented phantom scalar commands. Post-fix linked verification passes."
